{"parentUuid":"b71d6440-cd83-44f4-9c31-ba79e9d55875","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_013Z1c9KFHgLxbDGtkFSw2Qc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have a complete picture. Here's a summary of what the switch would look like. This is a recommendation — let me know which shape you want before I implement.\n\n## Current situation\n\n`cli/cmd/entire/cli/dispatch_wizard.go:485-515` — `discoverAuthenticatedDispatchWizardRepos` shells out to `gh api user/repos?...` to populate the repo picker in the wizard's Cloud mode. It returns a flat `[]string` of GitHub `full_name`s and hard-depends on a local `gh` CLI that's logged in with scopes to list private repos.\n\nThe `/dispatches/generate` call itself is already served by the Entire cloud API (via `dispatch.CloudClient` at `dispatch/cloud.go`). The `gh` dependency only exists for the wizard's repo picker.\n\n## Target: `/api/v1/repositories`\n\nThe new Hono route at `entire-io-worktree1/api/src/routes/repositories.ts` returns the same repos, already scoped to the authenticated user, plus richer fields including `checkpoint_count`. Bearer auth is the same token we already use for dispatch.\n\n## Recommended refactor\n\n1. **New helper on the existing `api.Client`**, e.g. `api/repositories.go`:\n   ```go\n   type Repository struct {\n       FullName        string `json:\"full_name\"`\n       Private         bool   `json:\"private\"`\n       PushedAt        string `json:\"pushed_at\"`\n       CheckpointCount int    `json:\"checkpoint_count\"`\n       // ... other fields as needed\n   }\n   func (c *Client) ListRepositories(ctx context.Context, sort string) ([]Repository, error)\n   ```\n   Reusing `api.Client` gets auth, secure-URL enforcement, and JSON decoding for free (see `api/client.go`).\n\n2. **Swap `discoverAuthenticatedDispatchWizardRepos`** to call the new helper via `NewAuthenticatedAPIClient(false)` and map to `[]string` slugs (the wizard's current contract). The existing `listDispatchWizardRepos` var stays a function pointer so tests can still override it.\n\n3. **Fallback behavior**: if the token is missing or the call fails, the wizard already falls back to `discoverLocalRepoSlugs(ctx, currentRepo)` (`dispatch_wizard.go:230-232`), so the behavior stays graceful.\n\n4. **Small UX wins to consider**:\n   - Sort by `recent` (API default) is probably better than the current `gh`-side `sort=full_name`.\n   - Surface `checkpoint_count` — e.g. `entireio/cli (12)` — so users can see which repos actually have data to dispatch.\n   - Only fetches repos the user has linked in Entire, which is what the dispatch endpoint can actually answer for anyway (no more selecting a repo that returns `access_denied`).\n\n5. **Tests**: `dispatch_wizard.go` already uses an indirection var (`listDispatchWizardRepos`), so tests can stub without touching HTTP. The `gh`-specific test paths (if any) can go away.\n\n6. **Cleanup**: with this change, `gh` CLI is no longer required for the wizard. `setup_github.go` still uses `gh` for repo creation/auth — that's separate and stays.\n\nWant me to implement it this way? If so, two quick questions:\n- Should the picker label include `checkpoint_count` (my suggestion), or stay slug-only to match today's UX?\n- OK to filter out repos with `checkpoint_count == 0` from the picker, or leave them in and sort them last?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":638,"cache_read_input_tokens":90789,"output_tokens":1210,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":638,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":1210,"cache_read_input_tokens":90789,"cache_creation_input_tokens":638,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":638},"type":"m